            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0432" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1090</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-10-12T16:00:00+01:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 13, 4 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>478. On authority think hostilities between Turkey and Russia will commence soon
                    and that ex-German ships Goeben and Breslau, rechristened Midilli and Javaz
                    Sultan, with rest Turkish Fleet will attack Russian Fleet in Black Sea.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
